Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 00:48:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] patch 0233 -- opl3: ship DMXOPL-derived GM bank
 data/opl3bank.dat

Binary asset: the 128-program General MIDI OPL3 instrument bank consumed by
the patch-0141 loader (DOPL3v1 format). Replaces the 8-patch family-bucket
placeholder that sounds thin/clipped on real OPL3 hardware (g2k report).

Source: DMXOPL (DMXOPL3) by ConSiGno -- github.com/sneakernets/DMXOPL,
MIT License (repo LICENSE; GPLv3-compatible). Converted from the upstream
DMX OP2 (GENMIDI.op2) by scripts/gen-opl3-bank.py: voice #1 primary 2-op,
per-operator regroup, KSL|TL recombine, 0xF0 stereo bits, OP2 note-offset
-> patch[11] int8 transpose. File is 1548 bytes (12-byte header + 128*12).

Lives in the engine data/ tree so it auto-flows into the dist DATA payload
via the existing `cp -R $(NX_DATA_SRC)/.` step -- no Makefile change. Binary
patch precedent: 0035 (sprites.sif asset rename). Provenance recorded in
THIRD-PARTY.md. GPLv3 like all nxengine-evo derivative patches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
